  "raw_label": "postponed_or_procedural",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Subaida vs The Secretary on 9 February, 2024 Author: N.Nagaresh Bench: N.Nagaresh In The High Court Of Kerala At Ernakulam Present The Honourable Mr.Justice N.Nagaresh Friday, The 9Th Day Of February 2024 / 20Th Magha, 1945 Wp(C) No. 1130 Of 2024 Petitioner: Subaida Aged 50 Years W/O Hamza, Valiyakualthingal, Deshabimani Road, Dewaswomparambu, Elamakkara P.O, Ernakulam, Pin - 682026 By Adv V.V.Suresh Respondent: The Secretary Kochi Municipal Corporation, Kochi Municipal Corporation Office, Park Avenue Road, Marine Drive Kochi, Ernakulam, Pin - 682011 By Adv K. Janardhana Shenoy This Writ Petition (Civil) Having Come Up For Admission On 09.02.2024, The Court On The Same Day Delivered The Following: Wp(C) No.1130 of 2024 2 Judgment",
    "facts": "Therefore, the petitioner was unable to submit that affidavit before the Kochi Corporation. Thereafter, the petitioner had not received any notice or any intimation from the Kochi Corporation regarding this matter. 4. The petitioner filed a detailed representation before the respondent regarding this matter. Without any notice the Corporation Authorities are trying to stop her business. Hence, the petitioner is before this Court. Section 11 of the Street Vendors (Protection of Livelihood and Regulation of Street Vending) Act, 2014 provides that any person who is aggrieved by any decision of the Town Vending Committee with respect to issue of Certificate of Vending under Section 6 or cancellation or suspension of Certificate of Vending under Section 10 may prefer an appeal to the local authority in such form, within such period, and in such manner, as may be prescribed.",
    "arguments": ""
  },
